The '''Nikto''' were a [[humanoid]] [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]] [[Homeworld|native]] to the [[planet]] [[Kintan]] in the [[Outer Rim Territories]]. There existed at least four Nikto [[subspecies]], the [[Kajain'sa'Nikto]] (red Nikto), the [[Kadas'sa'Nikto]] (green Nikto), the [[Esral'sa'Nikto]] (mountain Nikto), and the [[Nikto Ijosap'sai]]. Many Kajain'sa'Nikto were employed by the [[Hutt Clan]] as enforcers during the [[Clone Wars]], and centuries prior, while several green and red Nikto served the [[crime lord]] [[Jabba Desilijic Tiure|Jabba]] the [[Hutt]] shortly before the [[Battle of Endor]]. Some Nikto were members of the [[Jedi Order]], such as the [[Gender|male]] Kajain'sa'Nikto [[Jedi Master]] [[Ima-Gun Di]].

==Biology and appearance==
{{Quote|You know what I love best about Kadas'sa'Nikto like you? It's your thick hide.|translated=1|Greedo, to Takvaa|<ref name="Galaxy's Edge 2">[[Galaxy's Edge 2|''Galaxy's Edge'' 2]]</ref>}}
[[File:NiktoGuard-TCWCEJtB.png|thumb|left|200px|A Kajain'sa'Nikto guard]]
The Nikto [[species]] had at least three [[subspecies]]: the [[Kajain'sa'Nikto]] (or red Nikto) and the [[Kadas'sa'Nikto]] (green Nikto) were both well-adapted to arid [[desert]] climates,<ref name="Nikto (Green)" /> while the [[Esral'sa'Nikto]] (mountain Nikto) occupied more temperate, lush environments.<ref name="Oplock" /> Another subspecies was the [[Nikto Ijosap'sai]], which were commonly mistaken for the [[Prae'tus]] species.<ref name="Beyond Victory" /> Both red and green Nikto were distinguished by their scaly, coarse skin and various facial horns and spikes.<ref name="Nikto (Red)" />

The mountain Nikto were distinguishable from the red and green Nikto as they had no horns, possessing fan-like facial "fins" instead.<ref name="Oplock" /> Green Nikto offspring were [[Reproduction|born]] from [[egg]]s, thus they were referred to as hatchlings.<ref name="Bibo">{{Resistance|Bibo (episode)}}</ref> This subspecies was incapable of blushing, as their skin only contained green pigments,<ref name="Mutiny">{{Resistance|The Mutiny}}</ref> and had a thick, stiff quality.<ref name="Galaxy's Edge 2" />

==History==
===Early history to the Imperial Era===
[[File:ImaGunDi-TtG2024.png|thumb|250px|rioght|Ima-Gun Di served as a Jedi General during the Clone Wars.]]
{{Quote|The Niktos served the Hutts for centuries. They've never had a truly independent government of their own. Hardly even a world of their own, really.|[[C-3PO]]|<ref name="Bloodline">[[Bloodline (novel)|''Bloodline'']]</ref> }}
The Nikto originated on Kintan.<ref name="Nikto (Green)" /><ref name="Nikto (Red)" /> Centuries before the [[New Republic Era]], their home planet was discovered and taken over by the Hutts, who effectively enslaved the entire race. Under this Hutt rule, Nikto were not given any freedom to form a government of their own, and effectively lost control over Kintan itself.<ref name="Bloodline" /> Some Nikto were appointed as guards and thugs for their Hutt overlords and became a common sight in most of their enslavers' entourages.<ref name="Return of the Jedi" /> The [[Galactic Empire]] brought oppression down on the Nikto species during its [[Imperial Era|control]] over [[the galaxy]], with later stories warning the post-Imperial generations of how [[stormtrooper]]s treated their species.<ref name="The First Order Occupation">{{Resistance|The First Order Occupation}}</ref>

===New Republic===
[[File:KintanStriders-BoBFCh4.png|thumb|left|300px|The biker gang known as the Kintan Striders]]
Some time after the death of Jabba the Hutt, the Niktos managed to break free from their oppressors and at least one Nikto cartel existed during the New Republic's existence. It was led by a Kajain'sa'Nikto named [[Rinnrivin Di]].<ref name="Bloodline" /> A gang of Nikto [[Speeder bike|bikers]] known as the [[Kintan Striders Gang|Kintan Striders]] raided local [[moisture farm]]s around [[Tosche Station]] until they were [[Attack on the Kintan Striders|eliminated]] by [[Boba Fett]]<ref name="The Gathering Storm">{{BOBF|Chapter 4: The Gathering Storm}}</ref> around [[9 ABY]].<ref name="9 ABY date">The flashbacks of "[[Chapter 4: The Gathering Storm]]" occur shortly before the [[Attack on Jabba's Palace (Boba Fett)|attack on Jabba's Palace]], which "[[Jabba the Hutt and Other Characters of the Underworld]]" dates to around [[9 ABY]].</ref>

Some 30-odd years later, the young male Kadas'sa'Nikto [[Neeku Vozo]] served as a mechanic at [[Jarek Yeager's Repair Station|Yeager's Repairs]], a garage bay aboard the [[Colossus]] run by [[Team Fireball|Team]] ''[[Fireball]]''.<ref name="Recruit">{{Resistance|The Recruit}}</ref> He would later be promoted as the Colossus' chief engineer, once the station left its home planet of [[Castilon]], [[Hunt for the Colossus|pursued]] by the [[First Order]].<ref name="No Escape 2">{{Resistance|No Escape: Part 2}}</ref>

During the cat-and-mouse chase of the next months, the Colossus happened upon another Nikto in the person of [[Nenavakasa Nalor|Nenavakasa "Nena" Nalor]], a female of unknown subspecies. After socializing with the station's inhabitants and helping with repairs, which were abundant, Nalor's real motives were [[Sabotage of the Colossus|revealed]] upon investigation of her ship, which she claimed had barely survived a First Order attack. Nalor had in fact been hired by the First Order to infiltrate the Colossus and sabotage it, so that Commander Pyre and Agent Tierny could finally get their hands on the refueling station they had been after for too long. The plan failed, however, due to the quick thinking and rapid fixes performed by Vozo, resident engineer of the Colossus. Nena fled the station, and her failure was taken by the First Order with a sentence of her summary execution should they ever encounter her again.<ref name="The Engineer">{{Resistance|The Engineer}}</ref>

